  "facts": [
    "The Brooklyn–Battery Tunnel, opened May 25, 1950, stretches 9,117 feet, making it North America’s longest continuous underwater vehicular tunnel and the second‑longest worldwide at its debut.",
    "Designed by chief engineer Ole Singstad and later refined by Ralph Smillie, the tunnel’s ventilation system boasts 53 eight‑foot fans that can refresh the air every 90 seconds.",
    "Renamed in 2012 after former Governor Hugh Carey, the tunnel carries the entire unsigned Interstate 478 and averages 54,076 vehicles each weekday, including 28 express bus routes."
